<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Inference Time</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The inference runtime of most diffusion models is higher compared to regression approaches that only require a single forward pass. However, the runtime of numerical methods is magnitudes higher due to extensive collision checking and iterative trajectory optimization.
During data generation, we fixed the planning time to 20 seconds to achieve an acceptable success rate of the numerical planner.
We report the average runtime for our motion planning architecture as well as the individual ratio of model inference runtime and collision checking runtime in Table <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.1 Inference Time ‣ 4 Results ‣ Keypoint-based Diffusion for Robotic Motion Planning on the NICOL Robot" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The diffusion model has an average runtime of approximately 2 seconds, showing a very small variance, while the collision check has a runtime of 1 second.</p>
</div>
